Everything visible in a Flutter application is built from widgets. Prefer composing small widgets instead of creating very large widget trees inside one `build()` method.

### Stateless widget

```dart
class WelcomeText extends StatelessWidget {
  const WelcomeText({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return const Text('Welcome');
  }
}
```

### Stateful widget

Use `StatefulWidget` when the widget owns mutable UI state.

```dart
class Counter extends StatefulWidget {
  const Counter({super.key});

  @override
  State<Counter> createState() => _CounterState();
}
```

Prefer extracting repeated or conceptually independent UI into reusable widgets.

> [!NOTE]
> A widget should ideally have one clear responsibility. If a screen becomes difficult to read, extract meaningful sections into widgets.

content.es:
Todo lo visible en una aplicación Flutter está construido mediante widgets. Es preferible componer widgets pequeños en lugar de crear árboles enormes dentro de un único método `build()`.

### Stateless widget

```dart
class WelcomeText extends StatelessWidget {
  const WelcomeText({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return const Text('Welcome');
  }
}
```

### Stateful widget

Utiliza `StatefulWidget` cuando el widget sea responsable de un estado mutable de la interfaz.

```dart
class Counter extends StatefulWidget {
  const Counter({super.key});

  @override
  State<Counter> createState() => _CounterState();
}
```

Extrae las partes repetidas o conceptualmente independientes de la interfaz a widgets reutilizables.

> [!NOTE]
> Un widget debería tener idealmente una única responsabilidad. Si una pantalla empieza a ser difícil de leer, extrae secciones significativas a widgets independientes.

